description:
FOUND (s526w1, HTTP-Message t/message.t rows 86/87: `is(${$m->content_ref}, $foo)` got '' / '0' where perl gets the ARRAY ref).

Probe (scratch p-cast2.pl):
  my $x = [7, 8]; my $r = \$x;
  print $$r, "\n"; print ${\$x}, "\n";
  my @l = (${\$x}); print scalar(@l), "\n";
  sub n { scalar(@_) } print n(${\$x}), " ", n($$r), "\n";
perl 5.40.3: ARRAY(0x..) / ARRAY(0x..) / 1 / 1 1.   PCL (base 706cfde8 and tree): ARRAY(0x1) / 78 / 2 / 2 1.
Emission: both spellings are `(p-cast-$ X :rvalue)`; with X = `$r` (a box) the result is right, with X = `(p-backslash $x)` or a sub's return value (a raw ref value) cl/pcl-runtime.lisp p-cast-$'s (p-box-p inner) arm returns (p-box-value inner) -- the bare array vector, whose ref-ness lives on the CELL -- and the list consumer spreads it as an array.  The symbolic-ref arm in the same function already answers the CELL for a ref-shaped value (#3394); the box arm needs the same rule (or the consumer must not flatten a deref result).  Rows: HTTP-Message message.t 86, 87.  Layer: cl/ runtime (full sweep + bench for p-cast-$).

SECOND SHAPE (s526w1, same function family -- the REF-to-REF chain): `my $a = \\\\\'foo'; my $b = $$$a;` -- refaddr($b) equals the FOURTH level of the chain in PCL, the THIRD in perl (scratch p-refchain.pl: perl "L0 L1 L2=b L3 / loop same", PCL "L0 L1 L2 L3=b / loop diff"): a multi-level `$$$a` in one expression unwraps one level more than two stepwise `$x = $$x`.  Rows: Data-Dumper dumper.t 79, 81 (`$b = ${${${$a}}}` for `${${$a}}`), 85, 87.
